  bootwright / cluster sign-on suspend
      Return one managed Ceph cluster's management gateway to local sign-in while its identity
      provider is down: remove its CephSignOn's oauth2-proxy service, wait until cephadm turns
      the dashboard's single sign-on off and reconfigures the gateway, Grafana, Prometheus and
      Alertmanager, then prove that the custodied dashboard admin password is valid and the
      gateway serves its own sign-in. Requires a completed apply that realized the cluster's
      CephSignOn. Runs over the verified administrative channel on the cluster's bootstrap host
      and never contacts the identity provider. Records the suspension in the context before
      changing anything; repeat an interrupted command to finish it, and a repeat over a
      suspended cluster settles. apply never turns a suspended sign-on back on; bootwright
      cluster sign-on resume does. cluster info --secrets --name <cluster> reveals the local
      logins. Refuses external Ceph. --yes skips ordinary confirmation.

  Usage
    bootwright cluster sign-on suspend [flags]

  Command flags
      --name  Select the exact object name (required)
      --yes   Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright cluster sign-on suspend --context lab --name storage
